            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Backpressure For Free"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "for await (const row of rows) {",
            "  await db.insert(row)  // throttles source",
            "}   // loop body time = the brake"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Generators As Stages"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An async generator is a Transform in disguise",
            "Legal directly as a pipeline stage",
            "Often clearer than a Transform subclass"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Readable.from(cursor())  // DB cursor",
            "Readable.from(pages())   // paginated API",
            "// any async iterable becomes a stream"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Iterator Helpers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "await readable",
            "  .filter(r => r.ok)",
            "  .map(r => fetch(r.url), { concurrency: 4 })",
            "  .toArray()   // also .take(), .reduce()"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Helper",
            "Gives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "map / filter",
              "per-item, concurrency opt"
            ],
            [
              "take",
              "first n items"
            ],
            [
              "reduce / toArray",
              "collect to a value"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Trade-off"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Object mode costs more per chunk — no batched Buffers",
            "But record-oriented code gets far simpler",
            "For raw bytes, stay out of object mode"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Memory Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ignoring write()'s return — memory grows unbounded",
            "Only shows in production, at scale",
            "Huge highWaterMark to fix slowness hides backpressure",
            "Collect-then-concat is a buffered read with extra steps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Wiring Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "pipe with no per-stage handler leaves dest open forever",
            "Missing push(null) or _flush — consumer hangs on end",
            "Callback twice throws ERR_MULTIPLE_CALLBACK",
            "Mixing paused and flowing loses chunks"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas & Cheat Sheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Timing Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Peeking with data, piping later — first chunks gone",
            "Fix: a PassThrough tee, or pause() first",
            "finish is not on disk — wait for close or fsync",
            "On req close, destroy the source or it reads into nowhere",
            "await inside a data handler = unbounded concurrency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Boundaries lie",
          "text": "A JSON object or UTF-8 char split across two chunks corrupts the parse. Buffer the remainder, or setEncoding."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Type Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Implement",
            "Key events"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Readable",
              "_read / push",
              "end"
            ],
            [
              "Writable",
              "_write / write",
              "drain, finish"
            ],
            [
              "Duplex",
              "both, unrelated",
              "both sides"
            ],
            [
              "Transform",
              "_transform, _flush",
              "output from input"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Defaults To Memorise",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setting",
            "Default"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "byte highWaterMark",
              "64 KB (65536)"
            ],
            [
              "object highWaterMark",
              "16"
            ],
            [
              "autoDestroy",
              "true"
            ],
            [
              "emitClose",
              "true"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Signals & Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "write() === false, wait for drain",
            "push() === false, stop until _read",
            "Readable: readable, data, end, close",
            "Writable: drain (repeatable), finish, close",
            "Error at any point: error, then close"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing An API"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "production code",
              "pipeline (promise)"
            ],
            [
              "per-record logic",
              "for await"
            ],
            [
              "throwaway script",
              "raw pipe"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Implementation Checklist",
          "items": [
            "push(null) at EOF",
            "_flush if you buffer anything",
            "Call the callback exactly once",
            "Never assume chunk boundaries"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "When NOT To Stream",
          "items": [
            "Small files — readFile is clearer",
            "Data you need whole anyway: sort, JSON.parse",
            "Memory: buffered O(n), streamed O(highWaterMark)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One pipeline callback beats N pipe error listeners",
            "Always destroy(err); never emit('error')",
            "Web Streams interop: Readable.toWeb / fromWeb",
            "Async iterators cover many cases with no stream class"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Final rule",
          "text": "A stream is a memory-bounded pipe with a backwards feedback wire. Break the wire, break the memory bound."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of NODE.JS STREAMS. fs.readFileSync('10gb.log') puts 10 GB in your RSS. A read stream holds 64 KB — and that number does not change no matter how big the file gets. Ten pages on the four stream types, the drain protocol, why pipe leaks file descriptors and pipeline does not, and the twelve production traps that only show up under load. Save it for the next time a Node process gets OOM-killed at 3am.",
